{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The fifth passage</b><br>שיפוח. רוח היום:" "הרי בתר. [They are] the mountains of Gedor [?], and the separation [is] like ויבתר אותם. n: Text uncertain; (ה)גדור read tentatively as a place name; Ibn Ezra may be identifying הרי בתר with known biblical locales." "<b>The second passage</b><br>And you, my beloved — until שיפוח רוח היום — and this will be after the turning of the shadows, which is midday — return to your place:" "The beloved went on his way." "<b>The third passage</b><br>עד שיפוח היום על הרי בתר. For He said, 'for I will not go up in your midst,' and Moses would take the tent and pitch it for himself outside the camp."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:10.873028679Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}